From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:50:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 70/86] Split view: scrolling the preview scrolls the editor
 too

Scroll sync in the Split view now runs both ways. When the user scrolls
the preview (wheel, keys, scrollbar), the editor scrolls so the source
line drawn at the preview's top is its top line; the cursor stays. A
scroll the app started itself (the editor leading, a tab shown again)
is recognised by its target offset and not sent back, and a change of
the preview's size is not taken for a scroll, so the two never fight.

The map between source lines and preview position is finer: each line
counts the lines it wraps to at the preview's width (from the reported
viewport width and font size), code lines do not wrap, and a table's
|---| rule takes no height. Long paragraphs and tables now map line by
line and row by row instead of as one block, in both directions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

